* CAPX - single-file export of the converted LTspice model (ngSPICE model library, NG-010)
* Export-Schema: ngspice-export/1
* Kind: subckt
* Catalogue entry: name=CAPX kind=cap output=cmp/cap/00000.lib
* Build: needs stock; ngbehavior=ltpsa required: False
* Build-Token: stock
* Grade (NG-006): valid_for=['dc'] builds=['ngspice-42']
* Valid-For-Basis: dc=conversion
* Pins (in order): p n
* Port: p function=- on_symbol=- internally_unconnected=no source=SPICE subcircuit port order
* Port: n function=- on_symbol=- internally_unconnected=no source=SPICE subcircuit port order
* Polarity: - model_symmetric=True basis=model body is linear R/L/C only: no polarity in the model; the part is polarized and its + terminal is not in the data (LTspice database row)
* Channels: package=- model=-
* Licence: Vendor model, copyright held by its owner; redistribution terms not established.
* Exported by tools/export_model.py (ngSPICE model library)

* SYNTHETIC body (SM-009 test fixture).
.subckt CAPX p n
C1 p x 100u
R1 x n 10m
.ends CAPX
